error[E0602]: `each` is a loop, which needs a block: `each { |x| … }`
  --> 2:6
   |
  2|   xs.each
   |      ^^^^

error[E0602]: `each` is a loop, so it's a statement; it can't be used as a value. To build a value in it, assign to a local declared before the loop
  --> 2:10
   |
  2|   y = xs.each { |x| x }
   |          ^^^^

error[E0602]: `each` takes one block parameter to loop over an array's elements, or two to loop over a map's keys and values
  --> 2:11
   |
  2|   xs.each { |a, b, c| a }
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

error[E0602]: `<<` adds to an array, so it's a statement, not a value
  --> 2:7
   |
  2|   y = xs << x
   |       ^^^^^^^

error[E0602]: `push` adds to an array, so it's a statement, not a value
  --> 2:10
   |
  2|   n = xs.push(1)
   |          ^^^^

error[E0602]: `last` reads its receiver twice, and this one has a call in it; assign it to a local first
  --> 2:3
   |
  2|   g.last
   |   ^

error[E0602]: `+=` would evaluate this target twice, and it has a call in it; assign what it's in to a local first
  --> 2:3
   |
  2|   g[0] += 1
   |   ^^^^

error[E0603]: a range is only a loop's receiver, `(a..b).each { |i| … }`, or a `when` value
  --> 2:7
   |
  2|   r = 1..3
   |       ^^^^

