   |   ^

error[E0608]: an empty hash is not supported yet: Grindlang has no way to write an empty map, so a hash starts with at least one entry
  --> 2:7
   |
  2|   h = {}
   |       ^^

error[E0609]: each branch of an `if` or `case` used as a value here must be one expression; its branches may hold statements only where it is the whole right side of an assignment or a `return`
  --> 2:18
   |
  2|   1 + (if c then y = 1; y else 2 end)
   |                  ^^^^^

error[E0609]: a `case` used as a value here reads its subject again for each `when`, so the subject must be a local or a constant; assign it to a local first, or make the `case` the whole right side of an assignment or a `return`
  --> 2:13
   |
  2|   1 + (case g when 1 then 2 else 3 end)
   |             ^

error[E0609]: this branch gives the `if` or `case` no value to assign: its last statement must be an expression
  --> 3:5
   |
  3|     y = 1
   |     ^^^^^

error[E0609]: `X` is a constant, which takes one expression, so each branch of the `if` or `case` giving its value must be one expression
